   "Northwind-negotiator": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final text makes the 8-per-100,000 exceedance a mandatory recall default but lets regulators substitute an open-ended 'equally protective' corrective action, which weakens S5. S2 sets a 5% permanent limit with per-model rates given to purchasers and regulators, but with no mandatory sales stop for models above the limit, which benefits Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10. S3's open-ended 'where technically feasible' retrofit escape and 24-month new-unit start are weaker than the answer-key benchmarks."
 },
